requirements.txt

Edge cases identified (and how we handle each)
Edge case	Seen in real data?	Handling
Brand reply's parent tweet is missing from the file (broken chain)	Yes — likely, given we're using a subsample-friendly file	Skip, count as dropped_broken_chain
Brand reply points to another brand tweet, not a customer tweet	Possible (retweets/cross-references)	Skip, count as dropped_not_customer_parent
Customer complaint that's actually a mid-thread reply, not an opening message	Confirmed — we saw this last turn	Keep, but tag is_thread_root: false — filtered out downstream for taxonomy/golden-set use, still usable for grounding
Near-duplicate repeated complaints from the same customer	Confirmed — common pattern in support Twitter data	Drop repeats (exact match on normalized text), keep first occurrence
Message that's empty/meaningless after stripping mentions/links	Confirmed — e.g. "@Delta 😡"	Drop, count as dropped_too_short
DM-redirect reply (not a real resolution)	Confirmed — ~45% in our earlier sample	Keep the pair, but flag is_dm_redirect: true so retrieval can exclude it later — dropping it now would lose data other phases might still want (e.g. for volume stats)
Multiple response_tweet_ids on one row (comma-separated)	Seen in earlier sample	Irrelevant here — we only ever walk in_response_to_tweet_id backward, which is always singular

